# Code Size

## Limits

| Metric | Hard cap | Stretch max | Exempt |
|--------|----------|-------------|--------|
| Lines / file | 200 | 220–250 (edge case, <10% files) | `*.mock.ts` |
| Lines / function | ~20 | — | — |

Mock files (`*.mock.ts`) are exempt from both line limits and unit test coverage
requirements — they are temporary and will be removed when wiring real APIs.

## Proactive Component Splitting

Do not wait until a file reaches 200 lines. Proactive component splitting MUST be decided during Spec review:

- **Single Main Block** (e.g. 1 Table list): Use the standard page template without splitting.
- **Multiple Blocks (≥2 blocks)** (e.g. 1 Card + 1 Tab, or 2 Tables): Scaffold a separate component for each block; the Page file acts solely as an orchestrating layout. Tag each block with `#needs-component: WidgetName`.
- **Form Component Interlock**: Whenever a **Form** appears in the Spec (whether on a dedicated Create/Edit page or nested inside a Modal/Tab):
  - **[MANDATORY]** Extract the Form into a fully self-contained component (UI component, logic hook/composable, Zod schema, and Service client).
  - The component must be fully portable and reusable across contexts.
  - The Page file acts strictly as a host container.

Split in the same PR when exceeded line limits.

## Next.js ↔ Nuxt4 split convention

| Concern | Nuxt4 composable | Next.js hook |
|---------|-----------------|--------------|
| List data + pagination | `composables/xxx/useXxxList.ts` | `hooks/xxx/useXxxList.ts` |
| Column definitions | `composables/xxx/useXxxColumns.ts` | `hooks/xxx/useXxxColumns.ts` |
| Filter config + search/reset | `composables/xxx/useXxxFilters.ts` | `hooks/xxx/useXxxFilters.ts` |
| Export logic | `composables/xxx/useXxxExport.ts` | `hooks/xxx/useXxxExport.ts` |
| Form submit | `composables/xxx/useXxxForm.ts` | `hooks/xxx/useXxxForm.ts` |

No padding files with blank lines. Detailed component-split conventions are
product-owned because Nuxt and Next layouts differ.
